# Line-ending normalization (HEL-330).
#
# Git stores text as LF in the repo. These rules make the working-tree
# contract explicit and platform-independent, instead of leaving it to each
# machine's `core.autocrlf` setting.
#
# Why `eol=lf` on shell scripts specifically: with `core.autocrlf=true` (the
# default on the Windows dev setup), tracked LF scripts are smudged to CRLF on
# checkout. That corrupts the shebang (e.g. `#!/usr/bin/env sh` -> `sh\r`), and
# because the docker/api build COPYs entrypoint.sh from the working tree, a
# local `fly deploy` from Windows ships a broken entrypoint:
#   /usr/bin/env: 'sh\r': No such file or directory   (exit 127)

# Let Git auto-detect text vs binary, and store all text as LF.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must always be checked out as LF — the executable shebang depends on it.
*.sh text eol=lf
